<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The PowerPC recompiler emits code at runtime. Under the hardened runtime this
	  entitlement is what permits mmap(..., MAP_JIT), which is how xbyak_aarch64
	  allocates its code buffers.

	  Deliberately NOT present:
	    com.apple.security.get-task-allow
	        the debuggable-process entitlement. Its presence causes notarization to
	        fail outright. See Cemu.debug.entitlements for local debugging.
	    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
	        permits plain RWX mappings without MAP_JIT. On arm64 that is refused by
	        the kernel regardless, so it grants nothing and only widens the attack
	        surface.
	    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
	        existed to load an unsigned libMoltenVK.dylib. Vulkan is gone, and a
	        Developer ID build signs the executable and libusb with the same Team
	        ID, so library validation is satisfied without it. Note this does NOT
	        hold for ad-hoc signing, which has no Team ID -- see
	        Cemu.debug.entitlements.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
